# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: PDFS (the MTP filing system module).
Package: PDFS
Section: Disc
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-pdfs
Description: Phones, tablets and cameras (MTP) as discs
 PDFS, the Portable Device Filing System: an MTP device's storages
 appear as discs on the icon bar, for the Filer, *Copy and every
 program. The module goes into !Boot's PreDesk, so it's loaded at
 start-up; RISC OS 5's USB stack is needed. A beta: back up a
 device's data before using it with PDFS.
Build-Map: PDFS/PDFS -> ToBeLoaded/PDFS
Build-Map: PDFS/README.md -> Manuals/PDFS/README.md
Build-Map: PDFS/Testing.md -> Manuals/PDFS/Testing.md
Build-Map: PDFS/References.md -> Manuals/PDFS/References.md
Build-Map: PDFS/CHANGELOG.md -> Manuals/PDFS/CHANGELOG.md
Build-Notice: PDFS, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-pdfs/releases
